From 459e3dddd95a+11d72085cd39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ACK backport (hand-ported for OnePlus 6.1.141)
Date: Wed Aug 26 00:00:00 2026 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PM: drop WQ_FREEZABLE from pm_wq and wait in suspend_late

PM: drop WQ_FREEZABLE from pm_wq and wait for runtime PM in suspend_late

Two upstream changes combined and hand-ported for the OnePlus 6.1.141
tree, where the function is pm_start_workqueue() rather than
pm_start_workqueues():

- pm_wq is created with WQ_UNBOUND and without WQ_FREEZABLE, so runtime
  PM work is not frozen mid-suspend.
- __device_suspend_late() uses pm_runtime_disable() instead of
  __pm_runtime_disable(dev, false), so suspend waits for in-flight
  runtime PM operations instead of dropping them.

Source: AOSP kernel/common android14-6.1 459e3dddd95a, 11d72085cd39
---
diff --git a/drivers/base/power/main.c b/drivers/base/power/main.c
index 7716a2e..a46aefd 100644
--- a/drivers/base/power/main.c
+++ b/drivers/base/power/main.c
@@ -1382,7 +1382,12 @@ static int __device_suspend_late(struct device *dev, pm_message_t state, bool as
 	TRACE_DEVICE(dev);
 	TRACE_SUSPEND(0);
 
-	__pm_runtime_disable(dev, false);
+	/*
+	 * After this point, any runtime PM operations targeting the device
+	 * will fail until the corresponding pm_runtime_enable() call in
+	 * device_resume_early().
+	 */
+	pm_runtime_disable(dev);
 
 	dpm_wait_for_subordinate(dev, async);
 
diff --git a/kernel/power/main.c b/kernel/power/main.c
index 31547d8..01c4cda 100644
--- a/kernel/power/main.c
+++ b/kernel/power/main.c
@@ -917,7 +917,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(pm_wq);
 
 static int __init pm_start_workqueue(void)
 {
-	pm_wq = alloc_workqueue("pm", WQ_FREEZABLE, 0);
+	pm_wq = alloc_workqueue("pm", WQ_UNBOUND, 0);
 
 	return pm_wq ? 0 : -ENOMEM;
 }
